# 🟢 Level 1 – Beginner Explanation

# What is Malware?

**Malware** stands for **Malicious Software**.

It is any software intentionally created to:

* Damage computers
* Steal information
* Spy on users
* Encrypt files for ransom
* Disrupt services
* Give attackers unauthorized access

---

## 🏠 Real-Life Analogy

Imagine your house.

A burglar can:

* Steal valuables
* Secretly install cameras
* Lock you out
* Destroy furniture

Malware behaves in similar ways inside a computer.

---

# Common Types of Malware

| Malware    | Main Purpose                                             |
| ---------- | -------------------------------------------------------- |
| Virus      | Infects files and spreads when executed                  |
| Worm       | Self-replicates across networks                          |
| Trojan     | Disguises itself as legitimate software                  |
| Ransomware | Encrypts files and demands payment                       |
| Spyware    | Secretly collects user information                       |
| Rootkit    | Hides malicious activity and maintains privileged access |
| Adware     | Displays unwanted advertisements                         |

---

# How Malware Enters a Computer

Common infection methods:

📧 Phishing Emails

⬇️ Fake Software Downloads

💾 Infected USB Drives

🌐 Malicious Websites

📱 Fake Mobile Apps

📂 Pirated Software

⚠️ Unpatched Software Vulnerabilities

